WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:04.950
A lot of time has passed since Stargate SG-1
ended its run in 2007.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.200
Like most fans, you're probably wondering
what happened to the actors from the series

00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:10.500
since their days at Stargate Command.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.630
Here's what they're up to today.

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.700
Few actors have the honor of playing the main
role in one successful television show, let

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:20.900
alone two, but Richard Dean Anderson is a
member of this short list.

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.880
Anderson played the beloved protagonist of
the hit series MacGyver in the '80s and early

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:25.880
'90s.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:31.150
In 1997, he returned to television as Colonel
Jack O'Neill in Stargate SG-1.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.640
O'Neill is pulled out of early retirement
when the Stargate device is activated and

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.680
aliens come through attacking Air Force personnel.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.309
After a rescue mission, O'Neill becomes the
commander of the military unit Stargate SG-1.

00:00:42.309 --> 00:00:46.250
The team explores new planets through the
Stargate with the hopes of attaining new technologies

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.250
and allies.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:51.340
They need to put together a team capable of
defeating the powerful and sinister Goa'uld,

00:00:51.340 --> 00:00:54.040
who intend to enslave humanity.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:58.149
O'Neill frequently cracks sarcastic jokes,
even in dire situations, often bringing an

00:00:58.149 --> 00:01:01.649
appreciated dose of humor to an otherwise
serious character.

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:05.860
Despite his comedic side, O'Neill takes his
job very seriously, often risking his life

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:06.900
to save his unit.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.310
He is also deeply haunted by the death of
his young son, who accidentally shot himself

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.280
with O'Neill's pistol.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:16.860
After eight seasons, Anderson stepped down
as the main character and took on a smaller

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.820
role during the last two seasons as a guest
star.

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.840
After the conclusion of the Stargate SG-1
franchise, Anderson left the spotlight and

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.200
only appeared in a handful of TV show episodes
here and there, his last appearance coming

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.250
in a 2013 episode of the sitcom Don't Trust
the B in Apartment 23.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.680
While Anderson has attended several conventions
over the last few years, he largely remains

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:40.230
quiet about his personal life and has essentially
retired.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:44.350
Amanda Tapping played the intelligent and
overall exceptional soldier Samantha Carter

00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.920
for all ten seasons of Stargate SG-1, as well
as the two following Stargate movies and the

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.270
spinoff series Stargate Atlantis.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:55.810
Carter frequently struggles between choosing
a military career and a more scientific route.

00:01:55.810 --> 00:02:00.170
She's often the brainiac that explains alien
technology and phenomena to the audience.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:03.740
And she’s usually at odds with Jack O'Neill,
who wants things simplified.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:07.290
The show frequently teases a romance between
O'Neill and Carter, but the two are never

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.259
able to express their feelings due to military
protocols.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:14.040
"Normally neutrinos pass through ordinary
matter now matter how dense.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.060
I mean, something like five hundred million
billion just passed through you."

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:20.239
"No Matter how dense…"

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:24.439
Tapping continued acting, as well as directing,
after her Stargate years, and her talents

00:02:24.439 --> 00:02:26.819
are evident both in front of and behind the
camera.

00:02:26.819 --> 00:02:31.120
She starred in the sci-fi series Sanctuary,
as Dr. Helen Magnus and even directed quite

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:32.409
a few episodes.

00:02:32.409 --> 00:02:36.170
Tapping played the recurring character Naomi
in The CW's Supernatural.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:40.670
She’s even directed several episodes of
popular TV shows, including The Flash, Dark

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:43.480
Matter, The 100, Travelers, and The Magicians.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:47.530
Tapping remains very active and has plans
to continue directing, her most recent work

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:51.950
serving as an executive producer and director
for the supernatural TV show Motherland: Fort

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:53.299
Salem.

00:02:53.299 --> 00:02:57.299
Michael Shanks played the civilian archaeologist
Daniel Jackson, who originally argued that

00:02:57.299 --> 00:02:59.629
the Egyptian pyramids were built by aliens.

00:02:59.629 --> 00:03:04.219
When the SG-1 team assembled, he joined hoping
to one day rescue his wife Sha're, who had

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:05.959
been possessed by an alien parasite.

00:03:05.959 --> 00:03:11.280
While possessed, Sha’re ruled with her "husband"
Apophis as galactic dictators.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.939
Though Jackson doesn't have military training,
he can still hold his own, and often brings

00:03:14.939 --> 00:03:17.859
archaeological and cultural expertise to missions.

00:03:17.859 --> 00:03:20.669
It doesn't hurt that he knows over 30 languages.

00:03:20.669 --> 00:03:22.799
Jackson is the yin to O'Neill's yang.

00:03:22.799 --> 00:03:26.140
O'Neill is mission-minded and understands
the importance of obtaining technology to

00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:27.760
defend the human race.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:32.400
Meanwhile, Jackson wants to befriend and understand
all alien races even if they don't have technology

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.400
to offer.

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:37.079
This sets up a lot of internal conflict on
the team, though the two are always good friends

00:03:37.079 --> 00:03:38.479
at the end of the day.

00:03:38.479 --> 00:03:42.670
Shanks was in every season of Stargate SG-1,
but only had a guest starring role in season

00:03:42.670 --> 00:03:43.739
six.

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:47.370
He remained a very active actor after the
Stargate franchise, starring in the medical

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:52.099
drama Saving Hope as well as appearing in
several TV series such as 24, Eureka, and

00:03:52.099 --> 00:03:53.099
Burn Notice.

00:03:53.099 --> 00:03:57.769
More recently, Shanks joined the television
series Altered Carbon as recurring character

00:03:57.769 --> 00:03:59.419
Horace Axley.

00:03:59.419 --> 00:04:03.089
Christopher Judge played the alien Teal'c,
who was once the First Prime for the evil

00:04:03.089 --> 00:04:04.099
Apophis.

00:04:04.099 --> 00:04:07.339
Teal'c defected and helped the main characters
escape Apophis.

00:04:07.339 --> 00:04:11.599
He ended up swearing allegiance to Earth,
joining SG-1, and trying to free his people,

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:14.969
the Jaffa, from the clutches of their cruel
masters, the Goa'uld.

00:04:14.969 --> 00:04:18.519
Teal'c is comically serious, and often misunderstands
human lingo.

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:20.519
"Lucy, I'm home!"

00:04:20.519 --> 00:04:23.180
"I am not Lucy."

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.189
"I know that."

00:04:25.189 --> 00:04:29.319
He's an incredible tactician, often outwitting
enemies on the battlefield, and a very loyal

00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:30.319
friend.

00:04:30.319 --> 00:04:34.530
Unfortunately, his ethnic and cultural differences
often create conflict with upper military

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:36.860
personnel who question his loyalties.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.569
On top of it all, he often finds that these
same military brass want to "study" him to

00:04:40.569 --> 00:04:42.570
learn more about aliens.

00:04:42.570 --> 00:04:46.030
Judge went on to have a successful career
outside of Stargate, appearing in popular

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.210
TV shows like NCIS: Los Angeles and The Mentalist.

00:04:49.210 --> 00:04:53.280
Judge had a minor role in The Dark Knight
Rises and he was in the very campy movies

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.270
Mega Shark vs. Mecha Shark and Sharknado 3:
Oh Hell No!

00:04:57.270 --> 00:05:01.159
What you may not know, though, is Judge has
a very impressive voice acting career, particularly

00:05:01.159 --> 00:05:02.570
in video games.

00:05:02.570 --> 00:05:07.090
Most notably, he played Kratos in the popular
video game God of War, but you can also hear

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:11.599
his distinct voice in games like StarCraft
II: Legacy of the Void, World of Warcraft:

00:05:11.599 --> 00:05:15.800
Warlords of Draenor, and World of Warcraft:
Battle for Azeroth.

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.479
There was a large shift in Stargate SG-1 between
seasons eight and nine.

00:05:19.479 --> 00:05:23.219
Richard Dean Anderson took on a minor role,
leaving a big hole in the team we came to

00:05:23.219 --> 00:05:24.219
know as SG-1.

00:05:24.219 --> 00:05:29.259
To fill that slot, sci-fi veteran Ben Browder
stepped in as the new team's leader, Cameron

00:05:29.259 --> 00:05:31.370
Mitchell, for the last two seasons of the
show.

00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:33.400
Browder had previously starred in Farscape.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:37.629
He commanded a presence similar to the one
Anderson had on SG-1, both as a strong military

00:05:37.629 --> 00:05:41.189
leader and someone who could bring a laid-back
atmosphere to the screen.

00:05:41.189 --> 00:05:44.310
Mitchell is less sarcastic than O'Neill and
a little more optimistic and good-natured.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:49.190
Naturally, Mitchell's first challenge is smoothing
things over with a disjointed SG-1 and getting

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:51.360
along with all the other characters.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.919
Like so many other talented actors from the
series, Browder went on to have a successful

00:05:54.919 --> 00:05:59.930
acting career, appearing in TV shows like
Doctor Who, Arrow, Chuck, CSI: Crime Scene

00:05:59.930 --> 00:06:02.169
Investigation, and Criminal Minds.

00:06:02.169 --> 00:06:06.150
Browder also played the Sovereign Admiral
in Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2, and has

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:10.740
done a little voice acting for video games,
including Call of Duty: Black Ops III.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.970
It's been some time since we've seen him in
a leading role, but Browder remains active

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:14.970
today.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:20.310
In its later seasons, Stargate SG-1 featured
two actors from the sci-fi show Farscape.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:24.289
Ben Browder stepped into the male lead vacancy
left by Richard Dean Anderson, and Claudia

00:06:24.289 --> 00:06:25.819
Black played Vala Mal Doran.

00:06:25.819 --> 00:06:30.569
Believe it or not, Doran was originally planned
as a one-off character in season eight of

00:06:30.569 --> 00:06:31.569
SG-1.

00:06:31.569 --> 00:06:34.789
Doran returned in seasons nine and ten as
a main character and even appeared in the

00:06:34.789 --> 00:06:37.370
two movies The Ark of Truth and Continuum.

00:06:37.370 --> 00:06:41.389
Playfully mischievous and infatuated with
Daniel Jackson, Doran brought a dash of fun

00:06:41.389 --> 00:06:43.550
and moral ambiguity to the team.

00:06:43.550 --> 00:06:47.550
She joined Stargate Command in the fight against
the Oriwho are the new villains in seasons

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:49.960
nine and ten after the Goa'uld are defeated.

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:53.450
Since her Stargate days, Black has continued
acting in television.

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:57.189
She’s taken on the recurring role of Dahlia
in the fantasy drama The Originals, and a

00:06:57.189 --> 00:07:00.250
main role in the drama Containment as Sabine
Lommers.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.020
Black has also done a lot of voice acting
for video games and animated shows.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.050
You can hear her voice in Diablo III, Mass
Effect 2 and 3, Gears of War 3, Final Fantasy

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:12.020
XIV, and the celebrated animated comedy Rick
and Morty.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:17.360
"This will be the first instance of capital
punishment in our society in 500 years due

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:18.849
to our awesomeness.

00:07:18.849 --> 00:07:21.259
So we are forced to improvise.”

00:07:21.259 --> 00:07:23.819
She continues to act in television and do
voice work.

00:07:23.819 --> 00:07:28.219
Recently, Black played a role in the sci-fi
drama Roswell, New Mexico.

00:07:28.219 --> 00:07:32.440
Corin Nemec played a rather unique role as
Jonas Quinn, an alien from Langara.

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:36.150
Initially, Quinn was a minor character but
ended up becoming part of the main cast and

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.680
a member of SG-1 in season six.

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:42.539
Michael Shanks, the actor who played Daniel
Jackson, left the show during season six over

00:07:42.539 --> 00:07:45.539
creative differences, leaving a hole in the
main cast.

00:07:45.539 --> 00:07:49.270
As much as SG-1 fans loved Jackson, Quinn
helped fill the void.

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:52.919
Nemec portrayed Quinn as a scientist who brought
a quirky and fun spirit to the team.

00:07:52.919 --> 00:07:54.810
He was an immediate hit.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:58.840
Michael Shanks decided to return to SG-1 in
the following season seven, which made Jonas

00:07:58.840 --> 00:08:00.819
Quinn a minor character again.

00:08:00.819 --> 00:08:05.620
Corin Nemec continued acting after Stargate
SG-1 and remains active today, with a filmography

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:10.090
that includes guest roles on television shows
like NCIS, Supernatural, and Ghost Whisperer.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:15.520
In 2013, Nemec suffered an injury on a boat
while filming Poseidon Rex.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:20.529
His leg was shattered and required surgery,
but afterward, he healed and continued performing.

00:08:20.529 --> 00:08:24.590
In addition to acting, Nemec occasionally
writes and directs TV shows and documentaries.

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:29.520
Most recently, Nemec started touring the United
States filming a documentary called Love America

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:33.370
Tour, which focuses on unifying themes among
Americans.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:37.560
Teryl Rothery played the beloved medical examiner
Janet Fraiser, who faced the unimaginable

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:43.079
task of healing soldiers suffering from alien
diseases and wounds inflicted by alien technology.

00:08:43.079 --> 00:08:47.209
Basically, it's a whole new frontier of medical
science for humans, but she handled it with

00:08:47.209 --> 00:08:48.930
wisdom and optimism.

00:08:48.930 --> 00:08:52.430
Despite staying behind the front lines, Fraiser
occasionally saw some action.

00:08:52.430 --> 00:08:56.570
She went into the field a few times and also
had to deal with foothold situations in Stargate

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:57.570
Command.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.899
In season seven, the character died in combat,
although Rothery briefly returned to the series

00:09:01.899 --> 00:09:04.990
playing a parallel version of her character
in season nine.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:09.370
In addition to acting in over 70 episodes
of Stargate SG-1, Rothery acted in several

00:09:09.370 --> 00:09:13.519
well-known TV series, including Eureka, Supernatural,
Caprica, and Arrow.

00:09:13.519 --> 00:09:18.149
While she typically appears in sci-fi and
supernatural-themed TV shows, she's also taken

00:09:18.149 --> 00:09:22.900
a few roles in traditional dramas, particularly
on the Hallmark Channel, including Cedar Cove.

00:09:22.900 --> 00:09:27.950
More recently, Rothery appeared in the sci-fi
comedy show Upload and continues to play recurring

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.949
roles on The Good Doctor and Virgin River.

00:09:30.949 --> 00:09:35.080
Tony Amendola played the memorable Master
Bra'tac, the wise warrior who taught Teal'c

00:09:35.080 --> 00:09:36.940
everything he knows.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:41.470
Bra'tac is a retired military Jaffa on his
planet, but continues to secretly train others

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:45.380
because he plans to start a rebellion against
the Goa'uld, who are the slave masters of

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.380
the Jaffa.

00:09:46.380 --> 00:09:49.829
Bra'tac is a bit of a father figure to Teal'c
and is an important connection between the

00:09:49.829 --> 00:09:51.000
Earthlings and Jaffa.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:55.150
While these two species are technically on
the same side fighting the Goa'uld, they often

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:56.699
have cultural differences.

00:09:56.699 --> 00:10:00.130
And there's also the awkward fact that they've
both killed each other many times since the

00:10:00.130 --> 00:10:03.440
Jaffa are the soldiers for the Goa'uld.

00:10:03.440 --> 00:10:08.680
After Stargate SG-1 ended in 2007, Amendola
continued landing various roles in television

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:12.090
and also started voice acting in video games
and animated series.

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.600
He played a minor villain in the dark mystery
show Dexter, starred in the sci-fi series

00:10:16.600 --> 00:10:19.600
Continuum, and had a recurring role on Once
Upon a Time.

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:23.600
Amendola also appeared in CSI: NY, The Mentalist,
and Numb3rs.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:27.899
In addition to a successful career onscreen,
Amendola also has an impressive voice acting

00:10:27.899 --> 00:10:28.899
career.

00:10:28.899 --> 00:10:32.480
You can hear his voice in video games like
Star Wars Jedi: Fallen Order, Final Fantasy

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:37.529
XV, Fallout 4, World of Warcraft: Legion,
and Call of Duty: Black Ops III.

00:10:37.529 --> 00:10:42.410
He continues to act, mostly in television
or lending his voice to video games.

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:46.690
Peter Williams joined the ensemble cast of
Stargate SG-1 as the appalling Apophis, who

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:49.970
would serve as the main antagonist for the
first half of the show.

00:10:49.970 --> 00:10:53.850
Not only is Apophis a tyrant that enslaves
and murders humans, but he also has a unique

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:56.420
connection with several of our beloved characters.

00:10:56.420 --> 00:11:00.760
Teal'c served under Apophis as his First Prime
before defecting to Earth, but naturally,

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.981
those days haunt Teal'c.

00:11:02.366 --> 00:11:07.288
It doesn't help that Apophis exiled his wife and child, and enslaved his people, the Jaffa.

00:11:07.288 --> 00:11:10.959
 Apophis also took Daniel
Jackson's wife, Sha're, as a host for his

00:11:10.959 --> 00:11:11.959
queen.

00:11:11.959 --> 00:11:14.860
When he needed a host for his son, Apophis
kidnapped Skaara, who is like a

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.440
son to O'Neill.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.850
After playing the sinister Apophis, Williams
continued acting primarily in television,

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:24.180
appearing in the early 2000s Twilight Zone
revival and Fallen.

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:28.060
Williams continues to act, mostly in television,
and recently took on a role in the sci-fi

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:30.600
series The Expanse.

00:11:30.600 --> 00:11:33.740
Don S. Davis played the altruistic General
George Hammond.

00:11:33.740 --> 00:11:38.060
He's a loyal, no-soldier-left-behind leader
and frequently goes to bat for SG-1, even

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:39.800
when they break the rules.

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.940
Despite his strong leadership, Hammond has
a bit of a soft side.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:46.800
His two granddaughters are number one on his
speed dial, above even the President of the

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.130
United States.

00:11:48.130 --> 00:11:52.940
Unfortunately, Davis didn't live long after
the end of Stargate SG-1, passing away in

00:11:52.940 --> 00:11:55.009
2008 at the age of 65.

00:11:55.009 --> 00:11:59.430
At the end of the seventh season, Davis stepped
down as a regular actor on the show for health

00:11:59.430 --> 00:12:02.300
reasons and only appeared as a guest from
then on.

00:12:02.300 --> 00:12:06.139
Despite slowing his career down a bit, Davis
continued booking small-screen roles like

00:12:06.139 --> 00:12:08.190
so many of his fellow cast members.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:12.720
He appeared in the pilot episode of Psych
and the video-game-turned-movie Far Cry.

